# Line endings
#
# The specs.md framework scripts read YAML frontmatter with the pattern
#
#     content.match(/^---\n([\s\S]+?)\n---/)
#
# which requires LF. With `core.autocrlf=true` (this host's default),
# Git checks text files out with CRLF, which does NOT match — so
# `extractFrontmatter` returns null and the framework scripts report
# "Invalid ... frontmatter, skipping" and move on.
#
# The consequence is silent and serious: a unit brief's `status` is never
# updated to `complete`, and the intent's status never advances. A bolt
# completion would report success while leaving the memory bank claiming
# the work is unfinished.
#
# The memory bank is therefore pinned to LF in the repository itself, so
# the normalisation survives a clone on ANY host regardless of that host's
# autocrlf setting.
#
# Normalising the working tree is not enough — Git would reintroduce CRLF
# on the next checkout. This file is what makes the fix durable.

# The memory bank: frontmatter must be LF for the framework to read it.
memory-bank/** text eol=lf

# Source and scripts: LF is the convention the codebase was written in.
src/** text eol=lf
tests/** text eol=lf
scripts/** text eol=lf

# Configuration files.
*.json text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.pdf binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite-wal binary
*.sqlite-shm binary
